  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "She enters the story after a family-council wolf-den investigation lasting more than ten days, returning to the Mo household on Qing Mao Mountain as Gu Yue Mo Bei’s blood-related sister and a rank two middle stage Gu Master. She is Gu Yue Mo Chen’s granddaughter, the only person who dares enter his study without knocking, and the one who reports that the wolves’ den is nearly full and that a wolf tide will come next year.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "char_gu_yue_mo_bei",
        "sys_gu_master",
        "char_gu_yue_mo_chen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is slightly tall, with a decent body figure and proper curves. She has a long face like a horse’s, inherited from the Mo bloodline, and is a middle-upper tier beauty. She wears a dark blue uniform and a red belt with a square steel plate engraved with 2.",
      "chapters": [
        32
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the Gu Yue clan, servants and academy guards address her as the Mo family’s young Miss,",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "fac_mo_family"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and she moves with rank two belt marks and an imposing aura after clan missions.",
      "chapters": [
        32
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She treats Mo Bei as the future head of the Mo family and later tells him she was only a vice chairman in her academy year, hoping he will take the chairman seat she missed.",
      "chapters": [
        50
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Mo Bei is beaten by Fang Yuan, Mo Chen orders her not to interfere in junior fights, warning that elder involvement would look like Mo family bullying.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She still seeks Fang Yuan out at an inn with servants, including Gao Wan, and follows him into the school hostel under clan rules that limit how many servants she may bring.",
      "chapters": [
        32
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gao_wan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the dormitory door she refuses to force entry once Fang Yuan stands on the student-protection rule, then leaves Gao Wan to watch him overnight.",
      "chapters": [
        33
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan kills Gao Wan and leaves a minced corpse at the Mo family’s back door, Mo Chen confines Mo Yan for seven days and forbids further trouble with Fang Yuan. In that study scene she argues for killing Gao Wan’s family to protect Mo reputation; Mo Chen rejects the method and settles the matter with confinement, thirty primeval stones to Fang Yuan, and expulsion of Gao Wan’s kin with fifty stones.",
      "chapters": [
        37
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-young-miss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the academy year-end examination, students name her with Gu Yue Qing Shu and Chi Shan as rising-star Gu Masters, and her Mo family group is the largest present.",
      "chapters": [
        82
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_qing_shu",
        "char_chi_shan",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later wording treats that camp as the Mo faction’s Mo Yan group beside Qing Shu’s clan-leader group and Chi Shan’s Chi faction group.",
      "chapters": [
        87
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_chi_family"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is rank two upper stage while Qing Shu is already rank two peak,",
      "chapters": [
        104
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "and crowd talk at the red steel Relic Gu bidding treats her and Chi Shan as the favorites who could match Qing Shu if they obtained the Relic.",
      "chapters": [
        113
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_red_steel_relic_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later ranks Chi Shan, Mo Yan, and Qing Shu together as fighters above his own early rank two strength, noting that each holds at least three battle Gu and hidden trump cards while he still has only two.",
      "chapters": [
        107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Of those three groups, Mo Yan keeps an investigative Gu Master stronger than Chi She’s Snake Communication Gu, and she has single-handedly completed clan wolf-den investigation missions many times.",
      "chapters": [
        133
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chi_she",
        "gu_snake_communication_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under wolf-tide pressure after Qing Shu’s death, she and Chi Shan advance from rank two upper stage to peak stage.",
      "chapters": [
        145
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Alliance slope she answers Xiong Jiao Man’s challenge by name and accepts the fight.",
      "chapters": [
        126
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rising-rank-two",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiong_jiao_man"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Mo Bei dies in the wolf tide, clan rules that favor male inheritance leave the Mo faction without an inheritor. Even if Mo Yan later reaches rank three and becomes an elder, her assets would not stand for the faction, and marriage would move them under a husband’s name. Mo Chen publicly claims he detained Fang Yuan for Mo Yan’s sake, saying she had begged him not to let Fang Yuan die on the battlefield, and offers to accept stripping of elder status. That cover is stretched and hard for the other elders to believe.",
      "chapters": [
        172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-faction-crisis-and-marriage-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He then presses Fang Yuan as the son-in-law who could inherit Mo faction assets through marriage to Mo Yan.",
      "chapters": [
        172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-faction-crisis-and-marriage-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan answers with extreme bride-price demands, including a hundred thousand primeval stones and ten rare rank three Gu, and is chased out.",
      "chapters": [
        174
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-faction-crisis-and-marriage-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He later returns to re-bargain, settles for a cut price with forty thousand stones in advance plus Pig Iron Gu and Afterlife Grass Gu, and leaves with the condition that marriage talk waits until those goods arrive and that he will not guarantee allegiance before then. Mo Yan accepts the marriage as a family sacrifice while still hating Fang Yuan and feeling no affection for him.",
      "chapters": [
        176
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-faction-crisis-and-marriage-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_pig_iron_gu",
        "gu_afterlife_grass_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan begins killing Gu Yue clansmen inside the blood barrier to feed Blood Skull Gu, Gu Yue Mo Yan rushes him and is split in half by his Chainsaw Golden Centipede.",
      "chapters": [
        198
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death-in-the-blood-barrier",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_demonic_blood_skull_gu",
        "gu_chainsaw_golden_centipede"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes the name as Gu Yue Mo Yan, with Mo Yan as the short form and young Miss as the servant and guard address.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The camp under Mo Chen is called Mo family and Mo faction in different chapters, with Mo Yan’s group named as the Mo faction’s fighting team at the year-end intake.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later unrelated Mo clan caravan leader also uses the short name Mo Yan; that figure is not this Gu Yue clanswoman.",
      "chapters": [
        693
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_mo_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No Chinese characters for her personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
